# VAT exemption (VATEX) — extrafield labels and contextual help
FacturelectVatexCodeLabel=VAT exemption code (VATEX)
FacturelectVatexReasonLabel=VAT exemption reason
FacturelectVatexCodeHelp=VAT exemption reason code (BT-121) from the VATEX code list, e.g. VATEX-EU-G. Leave empty to use the automatic reason based on the VAT category. Note: this code applies to ALL exempt lines of the invoice; leave it empty if the invoice mixes several exemption regimes (the automatic mapping then assigns a distinct code per category).
FacturelectVatexReasonHelp=VAT exemption reason text (BT-120) shown on the invoice. Leave empty to use the automatic legal wording.
FacturelectVatexHelpTitle=VAT exemption (VATEX mentions)
FacturelectVatexHelpIntro=This invoice contains VAT-exempt lines. The following legal exemption mentions will be transmitted automatically to the platform (EN 16931 standard):
FacturelectVatexColCategory=Category
FacturelectVatexColCode=VATEX code (BT-121)
FacturelectVatexColReason=Reason (BT-120)
FacturelectVatexOverrideActive=A custom value is active for this invoice or customer; it overrides the automatic reason shown above.
FacturelectVatexOverrideMultiWarning=Warning: this invoice has several exemption regimes, but a custom VATEX code is forced and applies to all categories above — which is most likely incorrect. Clear the "VAT exemption code (VATEX)" in the complementary attributes to let the automatic mapping assign a distinct code per category.
FacturelectVatexOverrideHint=To customise these mentions (e.g. medical exemption, specific regime), fill in "VAT exemption code (VATEX)" and "VAT exemption reason" in the complementary attributes of the invoice (priority) or the third party.
